Changelog: 25-11-2026 23:40:24

Added. Nexus Marketing for PS5, a development app, the twin of Nexus Marketing for BC-250 (owner, 25-11-2026). It
writes an article that presents the portal and every app in it, as a web page in the suite's Bazzite design. The
apps, their categories, their tile names and their marks come from portal/apps.toml. The words come from
nexus_marketing/copy.md, a line per category and per app, and the tests fail when one is missing. The license and
the disclaimer come from the suite's README. The development apps are left out. The page links to the latest
release, the wiki, the Portal Tour and GitHub. It shows stills of the portal from tools/portal_shots.py, one per
category and one of the Settings page. The hero's background is a drawn placeholder until images/hero.webp is there.
Preview opens the page in the browser as one file. Export writes it to a new folder. Screenshots takes the stills
again, and Text check checks copy.md. Publish writes the article into the website's folder, commits only its files
as "see the changelog" and pushes. Its caption counts the files that differ, and it is off while the website is up
to date. A globe beside the info symbol opens the website.
